=== B0: period of (lam/n)_3 on primary n (brute force) ===
  primary n with N(n) <= 5000: 2005 ; residue classes mod 9 seen: 9 (expected 9) ; inconsistencies mod 9: 0
  depends only on n mod 3*lam ? False   => exact period ideal is (9) [conductor of the twist]
  agrees with the supplementary law DR (1.5): True
  gamma_2^{003}((-2, -3)) - (lam/pi)_3 g~(pi) = 4.6e-16
  gamma_2^{003}((4, 3)) - (lam/pi)_3 g~(pi) = 1.4e-15
  gamma_2^{003}((-5, 0)) - (lam/pi)_3 g~(pi) = 6.7e-17
  gamma_2^{003}((7, 3)) - (lam/pi)_3 g~(pi) = 6.3e-16

